The wavelength calibration required making some template solutions first from esorex data.
This was done using the esorex_to_pypeit script. Then, the wavelength calibration was performed using the
reidentify method and ech_fixed_format=True. Then, the wavelength calibration was generated for each setup
and the resulting WaveCalib Calibration frame was placed in the PypeIt_Templates directory. For detailed
instructions of this procedure, see the decsription at the bottom of this README file.

The relevant information was collected in the uves_templ_pypeit.dat file, and these were all combined using
the ingest_archive script.

The following files generated here are now in the main Repo
with different names:

wvcalib_angle_fits.fits -> vlt_uves_angle_fits.fits
UVES_composite_arc.fits ->  vlt_uves_composite_arc.fits

###################
Instructions for generating the wavelength calibration frames:

Change the params in the default_pypeit_par

Set ech_fixed_format = False

uncomment the norders and orders parameters

make sure order_spat_pos is commented

run the reduction to get the edges file

Calculate the edges (see docstring in order_spat_pos and order_spat_width) and update:
   order_spat_pos
   order_spat_width
   spec_min_max
For spec_min_max, you will need to open up the Calibrations/Edges_BLAH.fits.gz file and manually see where the minimum and maximum parts of the spectrum are located for the leftmost and rightmost orders.

Set ech_fixed_format = True

Remove all files in the Calibrations folder, and then run the reduction to get a new edges file.

Copy this to the dev-suite folder
cp Calibrations/Edges_C_2_DET01.fits.gz ~/Software/PypeIt-development-suite/pypeitdev/wavelengths/vlt_uves/580/Edges_l.fits.gz

Run the esorex_to_pypeit script

Copy the resulting reidentify script over to PypeIt
cp vlt_uves_580l_1x1.fits ~/Software/PypeIt/pypeit/data/arc_lines/reid_arxiv/

Run the reduction again to get the Calibrations wavecal file and copy this to the PypeIt_Templates
cp Calibrations/WaveCalib_C_2_DET01.fits ~/Software/PypeIt-development-suite/pypeitdev/wavelengths/vlt_uves/PypeIt_Templates/WaveCalib_580l.fits
